<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 8</p>
  <h1>Causative <em>have</em> and <em>get</em>: show who organizes, who acts, and what is affected</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">A passive can hide the organizer: <span class="ex">The data was checked.</span> A causative adds the person responsible for arranging or experiencing the action: <span class="ex">We had the data checked.</span> Change the object to a person and the next verb form changes too: <span class="ex">We had an analyst check it</span> or <span class="ex">We got an analyst to check it.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">70–80 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">organizer → affected object → action</span>
    <span class="tag">have / get + object + participle</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Identify</b><span>Organizer, performer, affected object.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Frame</b><span>Service, instruction, effort, or experience.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Finite tense, object, and final verb form.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Report</b><span>Keep agency and evidence responsible.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can use <span class="ex">have / get + object + past participle</span> for arranged work and affected experience; contrast it with <span class="ex">have + person + base verb</span> and <span class="ex">get + person + to-infinitive</span>; distinguish a causative from a basic passive, a conversational <span class="ex">get</span>-passive, Present Perfect, possession, permission, compulsion, and assistance; control the causative across statements, negatives, questions, progressive, perfect, future, and modal forms; identify a relevant service provider without inventing one; hear linked and reduced U.S. forms; and produce a clear project briefing with documented responsibility.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered passive voice, active object order, two participles, and the get-plus-infinitive pattern before combining them.">
    <h3>Reactivate the passive and verb-pattern foundation</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Causative foundation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was inspected">was inspected</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the wiring">the wiring</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="written">written</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="stolen">stolen</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="to reply">to reply</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="replying">replying</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>A licensed contractor inspected the wiring. The wiring <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was inspected" data-hint="Make the affected object the passive subject and retain the past auxiliary." data-fix="The wiring was inspected by a licensed contractor.">choose</button> by a licensed contractor.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>In <span class="ex">The contractor inspected the wiring</span>, the active object is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the wiring" data-hint="Find the thing that receives the inspection." data-fix="The wiring is the object affected by inspected.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The past participle of <span class="ex">write</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="written" data-hint="Past Simple is wrote, but the participle after have is different." data-fix="write → wrote → written">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The past participle of <span class="ex">steal</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="stolen" data-hint="Past Simple is stole; the participle changes again." data-fix="steal → stole → stolen">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>After three requests, we finally persuaded the supplier <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="to reply" data-hint="Get plus a person takes a to-infinitive when it means persuade or manage." data-fix="We got the supplier to reply.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice: the same project through four agency frames</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Northfield Community Center reopening</h3>
    <p>The center will reopen on June 1. It arranged for licensed North Coast Roofing to inspect the roof on May 3. <span class="ex">The center had the roof inspected on May 3.</span> The roof received the action; the center organized it; North Coast performed it.</p>
    <p>The operations manager assigned the booking-page update to the IT team. <span class="ex">She had the IT team update the page on May 14.</span> The named person or team performs the base-verb action.</p>
    <p>The landlord agreed to replace an exterior light only after three written requests. <span class="ex">The manager finally got the landlord to replace the light.</span> <span class="ex">Got</span> presents a successfully achieved response and the context supplies the effort.</p>
    <p>A pipe burst on May 21 and damaged twelve stored chairs. <span class="ex">The center had twelve chairs damaged by the burst pipe.</span> This is an affected experience, not an arranged service.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated organizer, performer, affected object, achieved response, and unwanted experience before choosing a structure.">
    <h3>Discovery check: recover each participant and relationship</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Causative discovery choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the center">the center</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the roof">the roof</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="North Coast Roofing">North Coast Roofing</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the IT team performs the action">the IT team performs the action</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the response required documented effort">the response required documented effort</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an unwanted affected experience">an unwanted affected experience</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the landlord's roof">the landlord's roof</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>In <span class="ex">The center had the roof inspected</span>, the organizer is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the center" data-hint="The grammatical subject arranges the service." data-fix="The center is the organizer.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>In the same sentence, the affected object is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the roof" data-hint="This thing receives the inspection." data-fix="The roof is the affected object.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The documented service provider is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="North Coast Roofing" data-hint="The case file names the licensed company that performed the inspection." data-fix="North Coast Roofing performed the inspection.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">She had the IT team update the page</span> means <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the IT team performs the action" data-hint="A person or team after causative have is followed by a base verb." data-fix="The IT team performs the update.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="ex">Finally got the landlord to replace it</span> is appropriate because <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the response required documented effort" data-hint="Three written requests show that the result was not immediate." data-fix="Get plus person plus to-infinitive presents the achieved response; the context documents the effort.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><span class="ex">The center had twelve chairs damaged</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an unwanted affected experience" data-hint="A burst pipe caused the damage; the center did not arrange it." data-fix="The form presents an unwanted affected experience.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: choose the participant after <em>have</em> or <em>get</em></h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Meaning and focus</th><th>Pattern</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>arranged work, affected thing in focus</td><td>have + <b>thing + participle</b></td><td>We had <b>the roof inspected</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>achieved or conversational arrangement</td><td>get + <b>thing + participle</b></td><td>We finally got <b>the light replaced</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>instruction, assignment, or requested action</td><td>have + <b>person + base verb</b></td><td>She had <b>the team update</b> the page.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>persuasion, effort, or achieved response</td><td>get + <b>person + to-infinitive</b></td><td>She got <b>the landlord to reply</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>affected or unwanted experience</td><td>have + <b>thing + participle</b></td><td>They had <b>twelve chairs damaged</b>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>The grammar does not identify the performer automatically</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">We had the data checked</span> identifies the organizer and affected object, but not the checker. Add a <span class="ex">by</span>-phrase when the documented provider is relevant: <span class="ex">We had the data checked by an external statistician.</span> Do not invent a provider. If the person matters more than the receiving object, use the active causative: <span class="ex">We had an external statistician check the data.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="note">
    <h3><span class="ex">Have</span> and <span class="ex">get</span> are not perfect synonyms</h3>
    <p>Both can describe arranged work. <span class="ex">Have</span> is often neutral and works comfortably in professional reporting. <span class="ex">Get</span> is common in conversation and can present a successfully achieved result, especially with <span class="ex">finally</span> or an effort context. Do not claim that every use of <span class="ex">get</span> was difficult. Let the surrounding facts show effort.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You chose each pattern from participant type, focus, and documented effort rather than treating have and get as decoration.">
    <h3>Choose ten agency patterns</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Causative agency choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had the roof inspected">had the roof inspected</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got the light replaced">got the light replaced</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had Priya call">had Priya call</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got Priya to call">got Priya to call</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had its window broken">had its window broken</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had the report checked by Dr. Lee">had the report checked by Dr. Lee</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had Dr. Lee check the report">had Dr. Lee check the report</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got the invoice corrected">got the invoice corrected</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had the assistant send">had the assistant send</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got the owner to approve">got the owner to approve</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had repaired the roof">had repaired the roof</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The center organized a licensed inspection and did not inspect the roof itself. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had the roof inspected" data-hint="Put the affected thing before the participle." data-fix="The center had the roof inspected.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>After three requests, the manager successfully arranged the exterior repair. She finally <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got the light replaced" data-hint="The affected object receives an achieved repair." data-fix="She finally got the light replaced.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>As Priya's manager, I assigned her the client call. I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had Priya call" data-hint="A named performer follows have and takes a base verb." data-fix="I had Priya call the client.">choose</button> the client.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Priya was hesitant, but after we discussed the reason, she agreed to call. I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got Priya to call" data-hint="The context presents persuasion and an achieved response." data-fix="I got Priya to call the client.">choose</button> the client.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>During the storm, the center experienced damage it did not arrange. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had its window broken" data-hint="Use have plus affected possession plus participle for the unwanted experience." data-fix="The center had its window broken during the storm.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The provider's documented independence matters. The team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had the report checked by Dr. Lee" data-hint="Keep the report in focus and add the verified checker with by." data-fix="The team had the report checked by Dr. Lee.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The next sentence should foreground the named expert's action. The team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had Dr. Lee check the report" data-hint="Name the performer after have and follow that person with a base verb." data-fix="The team had Dr. Lee check the report.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The supplier issued an incorrect invoice; after one call, we arranged a correction. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got the invoice corrected" data-hint="The invoice is the affected object, not the performer." data-fix="We got the invoice corrected.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>The director assigned a routine email to her assistant. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had the assistant send" data-hint="Neutral assignment uses have plus person plus base verb." data-fix="She had the assistant send the email.">choose</button> the email.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>Approval came only after a revised budget and two meetings. We finally <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got the owner to approve" data-hint="The context makes effort and achieved agreement explicit." data-fix="We finally got the owner to approve the plan.">choose</button> the plan.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build tense and question form on the first verb</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The finite form belongs to <span class="ex">have</span> or <span class="ex">get</span>. The affected object stays between that verb and the participle. A time marker selects the tense; the causative meaning does not.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Time or clause type</th><th>Complete causative</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>routine</td><td>have / get + object + participle</td><td>We <b>have the alarm tested</b> yearly.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>finished past</td><td>had / got + object + participle</td><td>We <b>had it tested</b> on May 3.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>process now or arranged future</td><td>am/is/are having + object + participle</td><td>We <b>are having it serviced</b> tomorrow.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>current result of earlier arrangement</td><td>have/has had + object + participle</td><td>We <b>have had it repaired</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>future arrangement</td><td>will have + object + participle</td><td>We <b>will have it checked</b> Friday.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>modal arrangement</td><td>modal + have + object + participle</td><td>We <b>should have it checked</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Past Simple negative</td><td>did not have + object + participle</td><td>We <b>didn't have it checked</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Past Simple question</td><td>did + subject + have + object + participle?</td><td>When <b>did you have it checked</b>?</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Present Perfect question</td><td>have + subject + had + object + participle?</td><td><b>Have you had it checked</b>?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Three different jobs for <span class="ex">have</span></h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">We have a service contract</span>: lexical <span class="ex">have</span> means possession.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">We have changed the locks</span>: auxiliary <span class="ex">have</span> builds Present Perfect; the subject performed the change unless context says otherwise.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">We have had the locks changed</span>: the first <span class="ex">have</span> builds Present Perfect; <span class="ex">had</span> is the causative verb; the locks are the affected object.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You changed the finite causative for time and clause type while preserving object-before-participle order.">
    <h3>Control eleven tense and clause forms</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Causative tense choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have the alarm tested">have the alarm tested</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had the roof inspected">had the roof inspected</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are having the sound system tested">are having the sound system tested</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have had the elevator serviced">have had the elevator serviced</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will have the programs printed">will have the programs printed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should have the wiring checked">should have the wiring checked</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="didn't have the chairs repaired">didn't have the chairs repaired</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="did you have the roof inspected">did you have the roof inspected</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Have you had the alarm tested">Have you had the alarm tested</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had the team update">had the team update</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got the owner to sign">got the owner to sign</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have changed the locks">have changed the locks</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Every January, we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have the alarm tested" data-hint="The yearly routine takes Present Simple causative have." data-fix="We have the alarm tested every January.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>North Coast completed the service on May 3. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had the roof inspected" data-hint="Use Past Simple causative for the dated completed arrangement." data-fix="We had the roof inspected on May 3.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The technician is booked for tomorrow. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are having the sound system tested" data-hint="Present progressive can report a current arrangement for a future service." data-fix="We are having the sound system tested tomorrow.">choose</button> tomorrow.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The elevator service is complete and relevant now. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have had the elevator serviced" data-hint="The first have is the perfect auxiliary; had is the causative verb." data-fix="We have had the elevator serviced.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The print shop is booked for next Tuesday. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will have the programs printed" data-hint="Use future will plus base causative have, then object and participle." data-fix="We will have the programs printed next Tuesday.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The unexplained power loss makes professional inspection advisable. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should have the wiring checked" data-hint="A modal takes base have; the wiring receives the check." data-fix="We should have the wiring checked.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The damaged chairs were discarded, so no repair was arranged. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="didn't have the chairs repaired" data-hint="Past negative uses did not plus base have." data-fix="We didn't have the chairs repaired.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Ask for the date of the completed roof service: When <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="did you have the roof inspected" data-hint="Past question uses did plus subject plus base have." data-fix="When did you have the roof inspected?">choose</button>?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>Ask whether an alarm service has happened by now: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Have you had the alarm tested" data-hint="Present Perfect question begins with have, followed by subject and causative had." data-fix="Have you had the alarm tested?">choose</button>?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>The manager assigned the update to a named group. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had the team update" data-hint="Past causative have plus named performer takes a base verb." data-fix="She had the team update the page.">choose</button> the page.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">11</span><span>After two meetings, the owner agreed to sign. We finally <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got the owner to sign" data-hint="Past get plus person takes to-infinitive for the achieved agreement." data-fix="We finally got the owner to sign.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep causatives separate from nearby structures</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Structure</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>basic passive</td><td>affected subject; organizer not encoded</td><td>The window <b>was repaired</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>causative arrangement</td><td>subject organized work on an object</td><td>We <b>had the window repaired</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>conversational get-passive</td><td>subject undergoes a change or event</td><td>The window <b>got broken</b> in the storm.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>active get causative</td><td>subject achieved another person's action</td><td>We <b>got the owner to repair</b> it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>make</td><td>compel or cause</td><td>The rule <b>made us wait</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>let</td><td>permit</td><td>The owner <b>let us enter</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>help</td><td>assist</td><td>The guide <b>helped us (to) find</b> it.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Do not turn an affected person into a blamed organizer</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">She had her phone stolen</span> neutrally presents an unwanted experience. <span class="ex">She got her phone stolen</span> occurs, but it can sound as if her choices helped cause the result. When blame is unsupported or irrelevant, use neutral <span class="ex">had</span> or a basic passive: <span class="ex">Her phone was stolen.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Directives and persuasion carry social meaning</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Have your assistant send it</span> can sound like a direct instruction. Adjust power and politeness: <span class="ex">Could you have your assistant send it by Friday?</span> <span class="ex">Get her to agree</span> may imply effort and can sound manipulative if consent matters. State the legitimate process: <span class="ex">After we answered her concerns, she agreed.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You kept arrangement, passive change, active causation, permission, compulsion, assistance, and affected experience distinct.">
    <h3>Choose ten nearby meanings</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Causative boundary choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The window was repaired">The window was repaired</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="We had the window repaired">We had the window repaired</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The window got broken">The window got broken</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="We got the owner to repair it">We got the owner to repair it</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="made us wait">made us wait</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="let us enter">let us enter</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="helped us find">helped us find</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had her phone stolen">had her phone stolen</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Could you have your assistant send it">Could you have your assistant send it</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="We have changed the locks">We have changed the locks</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="We have had the locks changed">We have had the locks changed</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>No organizer is identified; only the completed affected result matters: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The window was repaired" data-hint="Use a basic passive when the affected thing is the subject and no arranger is encoded." data-fix="The window was repaired.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We organized the service, but another person performed it: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="We had the window repaired" data-hint="Add the organizer before have, then object and participle." data-fix="We had the window repaired.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>A storm caused the change; the window is the grammatical subject: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The window got broken" data-hint="This is a conversational get-passive, not get plus object plus participle." data-fix="The window got broken in the storm.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>After negotiation, we achieved a named person's repair action: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="We got the owner to repair it" data-hint="Get plus person plus to-infinitive names the actor and achieved response." data-fix="We got the owner to repair it.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The mandatory security rule compelled everyone to remain outside. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="made us wait" data-hint="Make plus person plus base verb expresses compulsion or direct causation." data-fix="The rule made us wait.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The owner gave us permission to use the side door. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="let us enter" data-hint="Let plus person plus base verb expresses permission." data-fix="She let us enter through the side door.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The guide assisted us with the route. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="helped us find" data-hint="Help plus person can take a base verb in U.S. English." data-fix="She helped us find the room.">choose</button> the room.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The police report records theft without blaming the affected visitor. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had her phone stolen" data-hint="Neutral adversative have presents the unwanted experience." data-fix="She had her phone stolen while waiting outside.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>Make a request less abrupt when speaking to a client: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Could you have your assistant send it" data-hint="The modal question softens the instruction while preserving have plus person plus base." data-fix="Could you have your assistant send it by Friday?">choose</button> by Friday?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>Our staff personally performed the lock change, so choose Present Perfect active: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="We have changed the locks" data-hint="No outside service is arranged; the subject performed the action." data-fix="We have changed the locks.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
