  <h2>Sound natural: keep the final action audible</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In connected U.S. speech, function words may weaken and consonants link across word boundaries. The lexical action in the participle or infinitive must remain recoverable.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Line</th><th>Common connection</th><th>Listening key</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>We <b>had the ROOF inspected</b>.</td><td><span class="ex">had the</span> may sound like /ˈhædə/</td><td>Roof is the affected object; inspected is the action.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>We <b>got it FIXED</b>.</td><td><span class="ex">got it</span> may link with a tapped /t/: /ˈɡɑɾɪt/</td><td>Fixed is a participle after the object it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>We <b>got her to CALL</b>.</td><td><span class="ex">get her to</span> may sound like /ˈɡɛɾɚtə/</td><td>To plus call follows the named performer.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>We’ve <b>had it CHECKED</b>.</td><td><span class="ex">we've</span> and <span class="ex">had it</span> link closely</td><td>The two have-forms signal Present Perfect causative.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>We had it <b>painted</b>, <b>cleaned</b>, and <b>checked</b>.</td><td>endings /ɪd/, /d/, and /t/</td><td>The participle ending helps identify each completed action.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read reduced had-the, linked got-it, get-her-to, present-perfect causative, and participle-ending listening check" data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the participant order and final verb form from five connected U.S. English lines.">
    <h3>Listen for the participant after the causative verb</h3>
    <p>Ask your tutor to read each line naturally twice. Choose the complete structure and explain what the object or person after <span class="ex">have/get</span> tells you.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Causative listening choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had the roof inspected">had the roof inspected</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got it fixed">got it fixed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got her to call">got her to call</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have had it checked">have had it checked</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="painted, cleaned, and checked">painted, cleaned, and checked</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="got her called">got her called</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“We had the ROOF inspected.”</span> The organizer <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had the roof inspected" data-hint="Recover had the before the affected object roof." data-fix="We had the roof inspected.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“We got it FIXED.”</span> The tapped link still represents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got it fixed" data-hint="It is the affected object between got and the participle fixed." data-fix="We got it fixed.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“We got her to CALL.”</span> The named performer requires <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="got her to call" data-hint="Listen for reduced her and to before the base verb." data-fix="We got her to call.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“We've had it CHECKED.”</span> The complete Present Perfect causative is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have had it checked" data-hint="We've supplies have; had is the causative verb before object it." data-fix="We have had it checked.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Tutor reads three participles with different endings. The actions are <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="painted, cleaned, and checked" data-hint="Listen for /ɪd/, /d/, and /t/ while keeping all three as participles." data-fix="We had it painted, cleaned, and checked.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    <details><summary>Tutor script and transcript</summary><ol><li>We had the ROOF inspected.</li><li>We got it FIXED.</li><li>We got her to CALL.</li><li>We've had it CHECKED.</li><li>We had it PAINTED, CLEANED, and CHECKED.</li></ol><p>On the second reading, keep the causative verb light enough for natural rhythm but make the affected object or named performer and the final action recoverable.</p></details>
  </div>

  <h2>Read a service record without inventing agency</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Northfield reopening file</h3>
    <p>The community center approved a June 1 reopening plan on April 4. It had the roof inspected by licensed North Coast Roofing on May 3 and the elevator serviced by Metro Lift on May 8. Both providers submitted completion certificates. The center had 240 programs printed by Lakeview Print on May 20.</p>
    <p>Operations manager Elena Ruiz had the IT team update the booking page on May 14. Staff installed the directional signs themselves on May 24. After three written requests, Ruiz got the landlord to replace the exterior light on May 18.</p>
    <p>On May 21, a pipe burst in a locked storage room and twelve chairs were damaged. The center had twelve chairs damaged by the burst pipe; it did not arrange the damage. The incident report identifies the pipe as the immediate physical cause but does not identify why it burst or assign personal responsibility.</p>
    <p>A technician is booked to test the sound system on May 29. On May 26, the accurate report is <span class="ex">We are having the sound system tested on May 29</span>, not a claim that testing is complete. The file supports each named provider, date, and role. It does not support replacing an unknown performer with a guessed name.</p>
  </div>
