  <h2>Practice delegation without exposing private arrangements</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to disclose a real home address, landlord dispute, legal service, immigration process, medical procedure, financial record, security system, employment conflict, damaged possession, theft, or power relationship. Use Northfield or a tutor-created project. Agency practice should clarify responsibility, not pressure someone to reveal private services or accuse a real person.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Agency map:</b> Use Northfield or another fictional project. Name an organizer, three affected objects, two documented providers, and one staff performer before choosing any causative pattern.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Focus switch:</b> Report one service first with the affected object in focus and then with the documented performer in focus. Explain why each version serves a different reporting purpose.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Effort switch:</b> Begin with a neutral assigned action using <span class="ex">have + person + base</span>. Add a legitimate negotiation context and reformulate with <span class="ex">get + person + to-infinitive</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Time switch:</b> Move one service through routine, completed past, current arrangement, current result, future, negative, and question forms without moving the affected object.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Evidence close:</b> Name a provider only when the fictional record documents one. End with one fact the causative establishes and one detail it leaves unknown.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: deliver a 90-second service and delegation briefing</h3>
    <p>Use Northfield or a new fictional project. Report two arranged services in different tenses, one service with a documented <span class="ex">by</span>-phrase, one active <span class="ex">have + person + base</span> assignment, one <span class="ex">get + person + to-infinitive</span> result with an explicit effort or agreement context, one task performed by the subject, and one neutral affected experience. Include a negative, a Past Simple or Present Perfect question, and one future arrangement that is not yet complete.</p>
    <p>Then contrast a basic passive with a causative, distinguish <span class="ex">have changed</span> from <span class="ex">have had changed</span>, and soften one directive for the relationship. Close with the documented organizer, performer if known, affected object, timing, completion status, and one unknown. Your partner changes one participant or time; reformulate immediately.</p>
    <p><b>Listener check:</b> Can the listener identify who organized, who performed, what received the action, whether effort is documented, whether the event was wanted, and which details remain unknown?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved agency, participant order, tense, active-causative form, passive boundaries, register, and evidence limits.">
    <h3>Seven final decisions</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The team had the data independently checked." data-hint="The team arranged the service; the data received the check." data-fix="The team had the data independently checked."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence matches the B2 exit-assessment arrangement?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team had the data independently checked.">The team had the data independently checked.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team had independently checked the data themselves.">The team had independently checked the data themselves.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team got the data check independently.">The team got the data check independently.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="We have had the elevator serviced." data-hint="Use Present Perfect causative for a completed service with a current result." data-fix="We have had the elevator serviced."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence reports a current result of an arranged service?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We have had the elevator serviced.">We have had the elevator serviced.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We have the elevator service yesterday.">We have the elevator service yesterday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We had serviced the elevator by ourselves now.">We had serviced the elevator by ourselves now.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Elena had the IT team update the page." data-hint="Have plus a named performer takes a base verb." data-fix="Elena had the IT team update the page."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence gives a neutral assignment to a named performer?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Elena had the IT team update the page.">Elena had the IT team update the page.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Elena had the IT team to update the page.">Elena had the IT team to update the page.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Elena had the IT team updated the page.">Elena had the IT team updated the page.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="After three requests, Elena got the landlord to replace the light." data-hint="The context documents effort, and get plus person requires to-infinitive." data-fix="After three requests, Elena got the landlord to replace the light."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which line presents an achieved response without claiming that get always means difficulty?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="After three requests, Elena got the landlord to replace the light.">After three requests, Elena got the landlord to replace the light.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Elena got the landlord replaced because get always proves difficulty.">Elena got the landlord replaced because get always proves difficulty.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Elena had to the landlord replace the light.">Elena had to the landlord replace the light.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The visitor had her phone stolen; the report does not assign blame." data-hint="Use neutral adversative have for the affected experience." data-fix="The visitor had her phone stolen; the report does not assign blame."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which report avoids implying unsupported responsibility?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The visitor had her phone stolen; the report does not assign blame.">The visitor had her phone stolen; the report does not assign blame.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The visitor got her phone stolen, so she must have caused the theft.">The visitor got her phone stolen, so she must have caused the theft.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The visitor had stolen her own phone by a stranger.">The visitor had stolen her own phone by a stranger.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="When did you have the roof inspected?" data-hint="Past Simple question uses did plus subject plus base have." data-fix="When did you have the roof inspected?"><p class="quiz-question">6. Which question asks for the completed service date?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When did you have the roof inspected?">When did you have the roof inspected?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When had you the roof inspected?">When had you the roof inspected?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When did you had inspected the roof?">When did you had inspected the roof?</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The record names the organizer and affected object; name the performer only if a source documents one." data-hint="Causative grammar alone does not reveal an omitted provider." data-fix="Name an omitted performer only when reliable evidence documents that performer."><p class="quiz-question">7. Which close respects agency evidence?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The record names the organizer and affected object; name the performer only if a source documents one.">The record names the organizer and affected object; name the performer only if a source documents one.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The causative form proves the most obvious contractor performed every service.">The causative form proves the most obvious contractor performed every service.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A by-phrase is impossible even when a signed certificate names the provider.">A by-phrase is impossible even when a signed certificate names the provider.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect: can you defend every participant?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the complete agency path</h3>
    <p>Complete these lines aloud: <span class="ex">The organizer or experiencer is...</span> <span class="ex">The affected object or named performer is...</span> <span class="ex">The final verb is a participle / base verb / to-infinitive because...</span> <span class="ex">The time is carried by...</span> <span class="ex">Get does / does not imply effort here because...</span> <span class="ex">The event was wanted / unwanted...</span> <span class="ex">The provider is documented / unknown...</span> <span class="ex">A more polite directive would be...</span></p>
    <p>Then move an affected object into performer position, or replace an arranged service with an unwanted event. Reformulate the whole sentence and explain why the final verb form or causative choice changes.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
  </div>
